  "history_feedback": "fixed recorded actions",
  "plan": "InstinctFlash plan for robbyant/lingbot-va-posttrain-robotwin\n  plan tier: NUMERIC\n  operating point: schedule {kv_refresh=2 + video=2 + action=4} | guidance {action=positive_only@1 [implied by mode], video=cfg@5 [inherited from the family default]} | cfg batching {batch-2 on 8 of 8 declared forwards (negative branch requested by video); batch-1 on 0}\n\n  skip   graph_capture              [BITEXACT  ] Thor capture performance is unmeasured for this family/operating point; retain the eager default pending a paired device measurement.\n  APPLY  engine_offload             [NUMERIC   ] engine placement selected: SM110: FP8 engine passes the declared dimension and denoise checks; action-horizon and observation/control compatibility still require validation\n         expected: Measure this checkpoint with matched views, action horizon, denoise steps and timing scope. The matched Thor study separates native capture, FP16 engine and FP8 arithmetic; it does not establish robot-facing Runtime parity.\n  skip   pi05_tf32_numeric          [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:pi05', 'declares:pi05_tf32_numeric']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   fsdp_elision               [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: world_size=1, so every FSDP all-gather is identity while still paying a flat-param copy and stream sync per unit per forward\n  skip   allocator_churn_elision    [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: closed-loop serving has a stable working set, so releasing the pool between control steps only forces re-allocation next step\n  skip   debug_dump_elision         [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: per-chunk tensor dumps do a synchronous D2H on the critical path and are not consumed by the serving client\n  skip   obs_decode_elision         [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: caller wants actions only; ['vae.decoder'] need never be resident or executed\n  skip   conditioning_prefill       [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: ['text_kv', 'negative_text_kv'] declared pure in ['episode'] scope, but recomputed on all 8 forwards per control step (kv_refresh=2 + video=2 + action=4)\n  skip   prompt_encoder_staging     [BITEXACT  ] no memory pressure on this device class (sm_110, 123 GiB): keeping the prompt encoder resident avoids per-reset PCIe moves and allocator churn\n  skip   ring_kv_addressing         [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: streams ['video', 'action'] live across control steps in a pool that is currently addressed by boolean mask, costing a host sync and a full-pool copy per layer per forward\n  skip   action_terminal_forward_elision [BITEXACT  ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: the action phase's terminal forward writes provisional K/V that clear_pred_cache drops before any forward reads it; its output is discarded by construction\n  skip   sm120_gated_residual       [BITEXACT  ] hardware: needs sm_120, device is sm_110. This is a DEVICE decision, not a model one.\n  skip   sm120_wan_stage2           [BITEXACT  ] hardware: needs sm_120, device is sm_110. This is a DEVICE decision, not a model one.\n  skip   conv_layout_ndhwc          [NUMERIC   ] engine placement: execution goes through the fused engine pipeline, which is not a torch module graph, so there is nothing for this pass to install into. It was legal here: two Wan VAE Conv3D subgraphs can choose NCDHW or NDHWC by measurement on this device; NDHWC changes convolution accumulation order, so the swap is NUMERIC\n  skip   cfg_branch_elision         [NUMERIC   ] dropped by caller via Plan.without(): streams ['action'] discard their negative branch while ['video'] force batch duplication; forwards that can drop to batch 1 \u2014 action: 3 of 4 (commit steps exempt: their K/V feeds the other stream's negative branch)\n\n  NOTE: plan is NUMERIC because of ['engine_offload'].\n        Any accuracy-neutrality claim for this plan requires a paired\n        non-inferiority run.\n        `plan.bitexact_subset()` is the largest configuration that does not.",
